{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":18,"code":"JOB","name":"Job","testament":"OT"},"chapter":34,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"JOB 34:1"},"Furthermore Elihu answered and said, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"JOB 34:2"},"Hear my words, O ye wise ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["men;"]}," and give ear unto me, ye that have knowledge. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"JOB 34:3"},"For the ear trieth words, as the mouth tasteth meat. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"JOB 34:4"},"Let us choose to us judgment: let us know among ourselves what ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," good. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"JOB 34:5"},"For Job hath said, I am righteous: and God hath taken away my judgment. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"JOB 34:6"},"Should I lie against my right? my wound ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," incurable without transgression. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"JOB 34:7"},"What man ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," like Job, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["who"]}," drinketh up scorning like water? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"JOB 34:8"},"Which goeth in company with the workers of iniquity, and walketh with wicked men. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"JOB 34:9"},"For he hath said, It profiteth a man nothing that he should delight himself with God. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"JOB 34:10"},"Therefore hearken unto me, ye men of understanding: far be it from God, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that he should do"]}," wickedness; and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["from"]}," the Almighty, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that he should commit"]}," iniquity. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"JOB 34:11"},"For the work of a man shall he render unto him, and cause every man to find according to ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["his"]}," ways. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"JOB 34:12"},"Yea, surely God will not do wickedly, neither will the Almighty pervert judgment. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"JOB 34:13"},"Who hath given him a charge over the earth? or who hath disposed the whole world? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"JOB 34:14"},"If he set his heart upon man, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["if"]}," he gather unto himself his spirit and his breath; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"JOB 34:15"},"All flesh shall perish together, and man shall turn again unto dust. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"JOB 34:16"},"If now ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["thou hast"]}," understanding, hear this: hearken to the voice of my words. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"JOB 34:17"},"Shall even he that hateth right govern? and wilt thou condemn him that is most just? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"JOB 34:18"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["Is it fit"]}," to say to a king, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["Thou art"]}," wicked? ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," to princes, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["Ye are"]}," ungodly? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"JOB 34:19"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["How much less to him"]}," that accepteth not the persons of princes, nor regardeth the rich more than the poor? for they all ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are "]},"the work of his hands. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"JOB 34:20"},"In a moment shall they die, and the people shall be troubled at midnight, and pass away: and the mighty shall be taken away without hand. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"JOB 34:21"},"For his eyes ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," upon the ways of man, and he seeth all his goings. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"JOB 34:22"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["There is"]}," no darkness, nor shadow of death, where the workers of iniquity may hide themselves. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:22"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"23","sid":"JOB 34:23"},"For he will not lay upon man more ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["than right;"]}," that he should enter into judgment with God. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:23"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"24","sid":"JOB 34:24"},"He shall break in pieces mighty men without number, and set others in their stead. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:24"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"25","sid":"JOB 34:25"},"Therefore he knoweth their works, and he overturneth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["them "]},"in the night, so that they are destroyed. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:25"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"26","sid":"JOB 34:26"},"He striketh them as wicked men in the open sight of others; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:26"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"27","sid":"JOB 34:27"},"Because they turned back from him, and would not consider any of his ways: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:27"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"28","sid":"JOB 34:28"},"So that they cause the cry of the poor to come unto him, and he heareth the cry of the afflicted. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:28"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"29","sid":"JOB 34:29"},"When he giveth quietness, who then can make trouble? and when he hideth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["his"]}," face, who then can behold him? whether ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it be done "]},"against a nation, or against a man only: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:29"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"30","sid":"JOB 34:30"},"That the hypocrite reign not, lest the people be ensnared. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:30"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"31","sid":"JOB 34:31"},"Surely it is meet to be said unto God, I have borne ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["chastisement, "]},"I will not offend ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["any more: "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:31"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"32","sid":"JOB 34:32"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["That which"]}," I see not teach thou me: if I have done iniquity, I will do no more. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:32"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"33","sid":"JOB 34:33"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["Should it be"]}," according to thy mind? he will recompense it, whether thou refuse, or whether thou choose; and not I: therefore speak what thou knowest. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:33"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"34","sid":"JOB 34:34"},"Let men of understanding tell me, and let a wise man hearken unto me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:34"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"35","sid":"JOB 34:35"},"Job hath spoken without knowledge, and his words ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["were"]}," without wisdom. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:35"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"36","sid":"JOB 34:36"},"My desire ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is that"]}," Job may be tried unto the end because of ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["his"]}," answers for wicked men. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:36"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"37","sid":"JOB 34:37"},"For he addeth rebellion unto his sin, he clappeth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["his hands "]},"among us, and multiplieth his words against God. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 34:37"}]}]}
